   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "Para preguntar, usa **Have you got…?** o **Has he got…?**. Respuestas breves: **Yes, I have** / **No, I haven't**.",
     "@en": "To ask, use **Have you got…?** or **Has he got…?**. Short answers: **Yes, I have** / **No, I haven't**."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Para negar, usa **haven't got** o **hasn't got**: **I haven't got a brother**; **He hasn't got any children**.",
     "@en": "To deny, use **haven't got** or **hasn't got**: **I haven't got a brother**; **He hasn't got any children**."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Con plurales y cantidades no especificadas, es frecuente usar **any** en preguntas y negaciones: **Have you got any brothers?** / **I haven't got any sisters**. En estas frases normalmente no se traduce.",
     "@en": "With plurals and unspecified amounts, it is common to use **any** in questions and negations: **Have you got any brothers?** / **I haven't got any sisters**. In these phrases it is not usually translated."
    }
   ]
  },
